# Per-member SHA-256 digests of the approved Silesia corpus, in `sha256sum`
# format so that `sha256sum --check` reads it directly.
#
# The archive digest in ./silesia.pin authenticates the download as a whole. This
# authenticates it member by member, which is a different and stronger property:
# it survives repackaging. A mirror that recompresses the twelve files into a new
# zip produces a different archive digest and the same twelve member digests, so
# with this manifest such a mirror can be accepted deliberately -- pass it as
# `--manifest ./silesia.sha256` -- rather than either trusted blindly or refused
# outright. It is also what makes an already-extracted directory verifiable, which
# `--verify-only` needs and which an archive digest cannot do at all.
#
# Verified on 2026-08-12 against the extracted contents of the archive whose
# digest ./silesia.pin records. Change the two together.
#
# `sha256sum --check` ignores `#` lines, so the commentary above costs nothing.
